# One worker per line: "username,display_name,password,experience,skills"
#
#   username      - login username, must be unique (existing usernames are
#                   skipped, not overwritten - this only adds new workers)
#   display_name  - shown throughout the app
#   password      - a plaintext temporary password (change it later)
#   experience    - years of experience, a non-negative integer (blank
#                   defaults to 0). Compared against a years-of-experience
#                   band if one appears in a task's required_skills - see
#                   the "Bulk-adding workers" section of README.md.
#   skills        - comma-separated, and may contain any number of commas
#                   itself - everything after the 4th comma is taken as
#                   the skills string as-is, e.g.:
#
# worker7,Worker Seven,changeme123,4,python,aws,docker
# worker8,Worker Eight,changeme123,1,react,css
#
# A row missing username, display_name, or password is skipped as invalid,
# and so is a non-numeric or negative experience value. Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Maintained directly by admins by editing this file on the server - not
# uploaded through the web UI. Copy this file to bulk_workers.txt (drop
# the .example) and fill in real rows, then use the "Import workers" button
# on the Workers page (admin only). That file is gitignored since it holds
# plaintext passwords - treat it like a secret and delete it once you're
# done importing.
